   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Turbeh Company for Economic and Tec</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Turbeh is a mission-driven impact investment platform focused on Palestine&#x2019;s agricultural and rural economy. It mobilizes blended capital to support agribusinesses and agricultural MSMEs that are commercially viable but systematically excluded from conventional finance.Using patient and flexible investment instruments adapted to politically constrained operating environments, Turbeh invests across the West Bank, with a planned expansion to Gaza, and a strategic focus on Area C. Its investments prioritizeenterprises that strengthen food systems, improve market efficiency, and create decent employment&#x2014;particularly for women and youth&#x2014;thereby advancing inclusive and locally rooted economic growth.

Turbeh was created to address long&#x2011;standing investment gaps that hinder the modernization and competitiveness of Palestine&#x2019;s agricultural sector. Conventional financing has not met the needs of smallholders, women&#x2011;led enterprises, and youth entrepreneurs operating in marginalized and higher&#x2011;risk areas. Turbeh&#x2019;spurpose is to bridge this access&#x2011;to&#x2011;capital gap by pairing flexible investment instruments with impact&#x2011;oriented technical support&#x2014;enabling investees to upgrade production, expand operations, professionalize management, and build long&#x2011;term resilience. Indoing so, Turbeh strengthens the sector&#x2019;s sustainability and enhances the overall performance of the Palestinian agricultural ecosystem</narrative>
  </participating-org>
